	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Keyword "agents" lists live abduco sessions (from `abduco -l`) and, on selection, opens a new kitty window running `abduco -a &lt;name&gt;` to attach. Closing that kitty window only detaches the client (abduco's default behavior on hangup) - it never kills the underlying session, so it's safe to close whenever.</string>
